{
  "about": "§28 (docs/multisig-machines.md): a test build never writes to production. `defaults` are vela_core::service_defaults::service_defaults() — the one source every shell reads (uniffi service_defaults_json, wasm serviceDefaults, the web's generated serviceDefaults.ts). `builds`: a build is a test build when any fact holds (BuildFacts::is_test_build). `optIn`: a VELA_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_WRITES value and whether it opts in (service_defaults::opt_in). `cases`: service_defaults::write_verdict(testBuild, allowProductionWrites, method, url, body); `refused` names the production host. A write is any method but GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, unless a POST's body is JSON-RPC asking only READ_RPC_METHODS. Replayed by rust/crates/vela-core/tests/production_writes.rs and by each shell's guard test.",
  "refusedKey": "common.testBuild.productionWriteRefused",
  "optInName": "VELA_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_WRITES",
